1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,045
This is the Science console.

2
00:00:02,945 --> 00:00:06,070
We've scanned the hulk, and this is its intel tab,

3
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:07,893
with one sentence on it.

4
00:00:08,793 --> 00:00:10,481
I wrote that sentence myself.

5
00:00:11,381 --> 00:00:13,572
It's one of six lines in a text file,

6
00:00:14,022 --> 00:00:16,109
and those six lines have a shape,

7
00:00:16,559 --> 00:00:22,020
the same shape as every quest, every person and every place you'll write in this course.

8
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:25,526
So today, we learn that shape once.

9
00:00:27,326 --> 00:00:29,343
This is the file your story lives in.

10
00:00:30,243 --> 00:00:33,106
The lines at the top start with two slashes,

11
00:00:33,556 --> 00:00:36,772
which makes them notes, and the game skips right over them.

12
00:00:37,672 --> 00:00:39,319
Everything else in here is a record,

13
00:00:39,769 --> 00:00:42,690
and a record is simply one thing in your story.

14
00:00:44,490 --> 00:00:46,461
There are five of them in this file right now,

15
00:00:46,911 --> 00:00:50,086
and by the time we finish today there'll be six.

16
00:00:51,886 --> 00:00:53,900
Start by finding the hashes.

17
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:57,218
There are eight lines that begin with one,

18
00:00:57,668 --> 00:01:00,366
and every one of those lines is a heading.

19
00:01:02,166 --> 00:01:04,088
They all have the same shape:

20
00:01:04,538 --> 00:01:06,732
some hashes, then a space,

21
00:01:07,182 --> 00:01:09,258
then a name in square brackets,

22
00:01:09,708 --> 00:01:12,278
and then a key in round brackets.

23
00:01:13,178 --> 00:01:15,324
That's the link you learned in Lecture Four.

24
00:01:17,124 --> 00:01:19,901
Now, the hashes tell you what's inside what.

25
00:01:20,801 --> 00:01:23,396
One hash is the title of the whole file.

26
00:01:24,296 --> 00:01:25,934
Two hashes make a section,

27
00:01:26,384 --> 00:01:28,480
which is a drawer for one kind of record.

28
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:30,853
Three hashes make a record,

29
00:01:31,303 --> 00:01:34,597
and four make a record that sits inside the record above it.

30
00:01:36,397 --> 00:01:38,870
So these two, with four hashes each,

31
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:42,054
are the steps of First Contact.

32
00:01:43,854 --> 00:01:45,891
Let's take one record apart.

33
00:01:46,791 --> 00:01:48,276
The heading gives it a name.

34
00:01:48,726 --> 00:01:50,979
Then comes what I'll call the fence:

35
00:01:51,429 --> 00:01:55,200
two lines of three hyphens, and everything between them.

36
00:01:56,100 --> 00:01:59,471
Inside the fence there's one fact on each line,

37
00:01:59,921 --> 00:02:02,628
a label, a colon, and a value.

38
00:02:03,078 --> 00:02:06,119
Those are fields, and they're what the game acts on.

39
00:02:07,019 --> 00:02:08,850
Below the fence is the body,

40
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:11,890
which is just a sentence for people to read.

41
00:02:13,690 --> 00:02:16,097
So that's heading, fence, body.

42
00:02:17,897 --> 00:02:20,535
You don't need to know what these four fields do yet,

43
00:02:20,985 --> 00:02:22,300
but have a look at the last one.

44
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:24,612
It points at another record,

45
00:02:25,062 --> 00:02:26,512
and it does that with a key,

46
00:02:26,962 --> 00:02:29,449
because nothing ever points at a name.

47
00:02:31,249 --> 00:02:34,856
Now see if you can find the same three parts here.

48
00:02:35,756 --> 00:02:40,255
One line inside this fence has no colon, and that's allowed,

49
00:02:40,705 --> 00:02:46,324
because the first line of a fence can be a single word that says what kind of record this is.

50
00:02:48,124 --> 00:02:50,564
Now here's a scan record, in the game first.

51
00:02:51,464 --> 00:02:54,735
This is Science again, with the hulk's scan tab open,

52
00:02:55,185 --> 00:02:57,313
and that sentence comes from this record.

53
00:02:58,213 --> 00:03:01,721
Its body is two lines that each start with a percent sign.

54
00:03:02,621 --> 00:03:04,885
Each of those lines is one reading,

55
00:03:05,335 --> 00:03:07,876
and Science gets shown just one of them.

56
00:03:09,676 --> 00:03:12,240
A quest's name becomes its line in the Quest Log,

57
00:03:12,690 --> 00:03:16,370
and its body becomes the words in the pane when the crew selects it.

58
00:03:17,270 --> 00:03:19,677
A scan record's name isn't shown anywhere,

59
00:03:20,127 --> 00:03:21,886
because that one's just for you,

60
00:03:22,336 --> 00:03:25,323
and its body is the reading on a Science tab.

61
00:03:27,123 --> 00:03:29,052
And a key is never shown at all,

62
00:03:29,502 --> 00:03:31,540
because a key is for the game.

63
00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:35,604
Here's the first edit, and it's to these words.

64
00:03:36,504 --> 00:03:39,535
This is the Quest Log, with First Contact selected,

65
00:03:39,985 --> 00:03:42,531
and the words in the pane are its body.

66
00:03:43,431 --> 00:03:47,007
So in the file, I'm changing the words and nothing else.

67
00:03:47,907 --> 00:03:50,360
A body can be more than one paragraph,

68
00:03:50,810 --> 00:03:53,512
and in Lecture Eight we'll write one that is.

69
00:03:54,412 --> 00:03:56,715
Today I keep this one to a single line,

70
00:03:57,165 --> 00:03:59,964
and I'm not touching the heading or the fence.

71
00:04:01,764 --> 00:04:03,341
Now I'll write one of my own.

72
00:04:04,241 --> 00:04:08,777
I start with three hashes at the left edge, and then one space.

73
00:04:09,677 --> 00:04:12,606
Next comes a name, and then a key,

74
00:04:13,056 --> 00:04:16,782
which is small letters and an underscore, with no spaces.

75
00:04:17,682 --> 00:04:20,166
Then three hyphens, to open the fence.

76
00:04:21,066 --> 00:04:25,007
Inside it I say whose reading this is, which is the derelict,

77
00:04:25,457 --> 00:04:29,599
and which Science tab it goes on, which is intel.

78
00:04:30,499 --> 00:04:32,528
Three more hyphens close the fence,

79
00:04:32,978 --> 00:04:37,904
and then comes the body, which starts with a percent sign and stays on one line.

80
00:04:39,704 --> 00:04:41,118
So that's six lines in all.

81
00:04:42,018 --> 00:04:43,378
And this is what they make:

82
00:04:43,828 --> 00:04:48,829
Science, with the hulk scanned, and a tab called intel with my sentence on it.

83
00:04:50,629 --> 00:04:51,961
Now notice what I didn't do.

84
00:04:52,861 --> 00:04:54,946
I didn't put a space in front of the hashes,

85
00:04:55,396 --> 00:04:57,844
I didn't type anything after the last round bracket,

86
00:04:58,294 --> 00:05:01,593
and I didn't press the Tab key in front of a field.

87
00:05:03,393 --> 00:05:06,175
There are three easy ways to get this shape wrong.

88
00:05:07,075 --> 00:05:10,766
The first is leaving out the space after the hashes.

89
00:05:11,216 --> 00:05:12,690
Then it isn't a heading any more,

90
00:05:13,140 --> 00:05:16,996
and my six lines become six readings of the record above.

91
00:05:17,896 --> 00:05:20,525
The second is one field pushed in from the edge.

92
00:05:20,975 --> 00:05:22,870
That glues it to the line above,

93
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:25,811
and now the reading belongs to nobody.

94
00:05:26,711 --> 00:05:29,411
And the third is two hyphens instead of three,

95
00:05:29,861 --> 00:05:32,236
which isn't a fence, so there are no fields.

96
00:05:34,036 --> 00:05:37,786
In all three cases Science shows the hulk with no intel tab,

97
00:05:38,236 --> 00:05:40,099
and the game doesn't stop to tell you.

98
00:05:40,999 --> 00:05:43,082
So when your record isn't in the game,

99
00:05:43,532 --> 00:05:45,645
look at its shape first.

100
00:05:47,445 --> 00:05:49,936
First I check that there are no squiggles,

101
00:05:50,386 --> 00:05:52,623
and then I run one command.

102
00:05:53,523 --> 00:05:56,984
I'm looking for a single word, and that word is clean.

103
00:05:57,884 --> 00:06:00,652
The next lecture is all about this command,

104
00:06:01,102 --> 00:06:04,485
and it would've caught all three of the mistakes I just showed you.

105
00:06:06,285 --> 00:06:08,130
There's one warning until then, though.

106
00:06:09,030 --> 00:06:11,619
If I put one hash where there should be three,

107
00:06:12,069 --> 00:06:14,354
it still says the word clean.

108
00:06:15,254 --> 00:06:20,265
That's because with one hash this line is a title, not a record,

109
00:06:20,715 --> 00:06:22,142
so the game never reads it.

110
00:06:23,942 --> 00:06:26,425
Clean only means the checker found nothing,

111
00:06:26,875 --> 00:06:28,737
so count your hashes yourself.

112
00:06:30,537 --> 00:06:32,998
I click the handheld, and then Quests,

113
00:06:33,448 --> 00:06:34,872
and this is the Quest Log.

114
00:06:35,772 --> 00:06:39,079
There's my new sentence, in the pane for First Contact.

115
00:06:40,879 --> 00:06:43,525
Now for Science, once we're close to the hulk.

116
00:06:44,425 --> 00:06:47,572
I select it, and its scan tabs come up over the map.

117
00:06:48,472 --> 00:06:50,222
One of them is called intel,

118
00:06:50,672 --> 00:06:53,537
and when its scan is done, that's my sentence.

119
00:06:55,337 --> 00:06:58,243
Give the hulk a fourth tab, with a record of your own.

120
00:06:59,143 --> 00:07:01,384
Then change the name of First Contact,

121
00:07:01,834 --> 00:07:04,272
and watch what changes and what doesn't.

122
00:07:06,072 --> 00:07:09,045
Next time, we'll break five things on purpose,

123
00:07:09,495 --> 00:07:11,071
and read what the checker says.
